a few moments ago Buckingham Palace  announced the death of her majesty Queen  Elizabeth II the queen died peacefully  at Balmoral this afternoon the world is  mourning the loss of Queen Elizabeth II  the longest reigning monarch of Britain  just before the announcement at 10 30  a.m Pacific Time a rainbow could be seen  stretching across the skies above  Buckingham Palace where crowds gathered  as the news rippled across the globe and  the Royals rushed to the Queen's bedside  at Balmoral Castle in Scotland Queen  Elizabeth's son Charles just named his  majesty the king released a statement in  the wake of the devastating news quote  the death of my beloved mother her  majesty the queen is a moment of the  greatest sadness for me and all members  of my family we mourn profoundly the  passing of a cherished Sovereign and a  much-loved mother I know her loss will  be deeply felt your majesty  Mommy  and now Stars throughout Hollywood are  remembering the Beloved Queen I often  draw strengths from meeting ordinary  people doing extraordinary things  Jennifer Garner shared this stunning  photo and called her an elegant  incredible woman  Elton John who was knighted by the queen  in 1998 posted a lengthy note to Twitter  reading in part quote she was an  inspiring presence to be around Queen  Elizabeth has been a huge part of my  life from childhood to this day and I  will miss her dearly  [Music]  never did  former president Barack Obama and his  wife Michelle remember her majesty as a  Beacon of Hope and stability quote  Michelle and I were lucky enough to come  to know her majesty and she meant a  great deal to us she welcomed us to the  world stage with open arms we are awed  by her Legacy of tireless dignified  public service  another former President Bill Clinton  spoke out giving thanks for the Queen's  extraordinary life  quote we will always be grateful for the  kindness she showed us through the years  life of course consists of final  partings Ozzy Osbourne Mourns the loss  he says England without the queen is  devastating  George Takei also shares his condolences  quote there shall be none other like her  sharing a similar sentiment Sylvester  Stallone who paid tribute to the great  Queen with a photo of their first  meeting I'm very glad to be able to join  you  [Music]  foreign  [Music]
 

